00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:00.893
- It's always nice
(audience clapping)

00:00:00.893 --> 00:00:03.300
to wrap up an hour with
something fun and surprising

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.230
from social media. This
is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.415
(intro music)

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:08.160
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.080
It's no secret we're getting hit big time

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.990
in our wallets these days.
Everything just costs more.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.190
Well, there's a very creative woman

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.660
on TikTok making the most of it

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.480
by up cycling clothes in
the most creative way.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.802
Just check out some of her
signature fashions right here.

00:00:21.802 --> 00:00:24.385
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.071 --> 00:00:31.289
(audience clapping)
- [Kelly] Man.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:34.530
That's Ariel. An outfit she
made out bags from retail stores

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.630
and TikTok is going crazy for it.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.790
We have Ariel on the line right now,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.390
watching on NBC for Los Angeles.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:43.500
[Kelly] Hello!
- Hi.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.240
- [Kelly] I mean, you're cool.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.520
I like, I can't do that
like, what you're doing

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.533
but how did you come up with this idea?

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.480
- So basically July, 2020
we were out of school.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.600
Outta sheer boredom, I
bought a sewing machine

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.520
and then a few days later a friend and I

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.890
went to IKEA 'cause he needed furniture

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.100
and he jumped around and
said I should make clothes

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.570
out of the bags we walked past.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.690
I was like, "Sure, why
not?" So, I bought the bags

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.990
and I made this outfit. I
made it in like, three days.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.970
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh. It
would take me three months

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.120
and it would look so bad.
So you say this isn't

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.560
about making a fashion statement though.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.170
It's it's a social movement
as, as well, right?

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.870
- Yeah, I think it's really important

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.450
for people to try to make anything

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.370
'cause you can literally make anything

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.353
out of anything in your house.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.040
And especially, the fashion industry,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.550
has taught us to buy things
and discard them all the time.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.880
And I think this is a fun way
to just kind of make clothes

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.240
for yourself and just have fun with it.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.412
- [Kelly] Absolutely.
(audience clapping)

00:01:46.412 --> 00:01:49.770
- [Kelly] It's super
cool. You're very gifted.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.893
Thank you so much Ariel. I'm
liking your post right now.

00:01:52.893 --> 00:01:55.350
(audience cheering)

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.750
And that's not all, our season
long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.550
